      "help_uri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield006.md",
      "line": 29,
      "message": "`ReplicatedStorage.Remotes.GetLocalCoins:InvokeClient()` makes the server wait for an answer from a client, which may never come",
      "rule": "luau-shield006",
      "severity": "medium",
      "slug": "server-invokes-client",
      "snippet": "\trecordFixed(target, ReplicatedStorage.Remotes.GetLocalCoins:InvokeClient(target)) -- expect: luau-shield006",
      "title": "Server waits for a client with RemoteFunction:InvokeClient",
      "why": "A malicious client can simply never return: the server thread yields forever (pcall does not help), leaking memory and blocking whatever logic waits for the answer. A client that errors or leaves also breaks the call, and every value it returns is client-controlled."
    },
