      "end_line": 30,
      "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/datastore-updateasync-transform.server.luau",
      "fix": "Missing: an upper bound and NaN rejection. Let the server decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == \"number\"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`) and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key.",
      "flow": [
        {
          "column": 66,
          "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/datastore-updateasync-transform.server.luau",
          "line": 18,
          "note": "`points` (parameter #2) of the `ChallengeComplete.OnServerEvent` handler is sent by the client (the type annotation `number` is not checked at runtime)"
