    {
      "column": 2,
      "end_column": 19,
      "end_line": 38,
      "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/validator-misses-nan.server.luau",
      "fix": "The range check does not reject NaN: every comparison with NaN is false, so `if x <= 0 or x > max then return end` lets NaN through (and math.clamp/min/max return NaN for NaN). Add `if x ~= x then return end`. Let the server decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == \"number\"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`) and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key.",
      "flow": [
        {
          "column": 53,
          "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/validator-misses-nan.server.luau",
          "line": 32,
          "note": "`bet` (parameter #2) of the `SpinSlots.OnServerInvoke` handler is sent by the client (the type annotation `number` is not checked at runtime)"
        },
        {
          "column": 2,
          "file": "tests/fixtures/luau-shield001/vulnerable/validator-misses-nan.server.luau",
          "line": 38,
          "note": "`bet` (client-controlled) is subtracted from `profile.Data.Cash`"
        }
      ],
      "help_uri": "https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield001.md",
